# spec_id: eravos.organism.fx-destroyer · version 2.0.0 · phase P8.1 · status canonical
# source: v10 plugins/dist.json + bitcrush.json "8-BIT DESTROYER" (shells, F-19) · inherits STD.fx
identity:
  id: eravos.fx-destroyer ; label: Destroyer ; icon: 👾 ; accent: "#aaff00"
  comp_intent: Saturation to total destruction — warm tape, grit, fold, fuzz, 8-bit crunch — that sits in a mix.
  novelty: Only FX with an AudioWorklet DSP stage (fractional sample-rate reduction + bit depth), series non-linear chain with a clean low band.
why_2_0 (measured, tests/tool-audio.mjs + the tool's own tests):
  - 1.x levelled the shaper at a FULL-SCALE sine: real parts (−12…−24 dBFS) came out up to +13 dB louder and squashed → now matched across −6…−24 dBFS (±6 dB at full drive, every shape)
  - hard / fold curves were brick walls (fizz) → own curves with a smooth knee; drive adds gain into the knee, folds capped at ~2.5
  - downsample folded every partial back as inharmonic hash (Total Destruction: alias +8 dB OVER the signal) → anti-alias + anti-image filters, ALIAS knob
  - bass went through the shaper full band (mud, sub lost) → TIGHT pre high-pass + LOW KEEP crossover
engine:
  chain: tilt → TIGHT HP (12 dB/oct) → LOW KEEP split (LR4; lows delayed by the 4× latency, so the sum is flat) → SHAPER (soft | hard | tube | fold | tape | fuzz | rectify, ASYM bias, 4× oversample) → makeup → DC block → anti-alias LP → CRUSHER worklet (fractional bits 1..16, fractional hold 1..64, TPDF dither) → anti-image LP (2×) → TAME LP (follows drive by AUTO TAME) → DC block → + low band → mix
  worklet: 'eravos-crush2', Blob-loaded (runtime precision-clock pattern) ; fallback: WaveShaper quantization only (downsample disabled, org:error notice)
  alias: crusher Nyquist fN = sr / (2·down) ; anti-alias at 0.9·fN·2^(4·alias), anti-image at 0.9·fN·2^(3·alias) (capped 0.92·sr/2)
  silence: curves have odd length with an exact 0 at the centre; the crusher passes |x| < 1e-5 as 0 (no DC step, no dither hiss)
config: shape enum [soft, hard, tube, fold, tape, fuzz, rectify] def soft ; drive 0..1 def 0.3 ; asym 0..1 def 0 ; autoGain bool def true ; tight 10..600 Hz def 25 ; lowKeep 0..400 Hz def 0 (off < 20) ; bits 1..16 def 16 ; downsample 1..64 def 1 ; alias 0..1 def 0.35 ; dither bool def false ; tilt −1..1 ; postLP 1000..20000 def 16000 ; autoTame 0..1 def 0.5 ; STD mix
presets: Tape Warm, Grit, Fold Growl, NES 8-bit, Lo-fi 12-bit 22k, Total Destruction, Bass Grit (parallel), 80s · SP-1200 Grit (12-bit), Tape Saturation, Fuzz Box, Octave Rectifier, Wub Grit · sub stays clean, Growl Fold · sub stays clean, Drum Bus Crunch, Cassette 8-bit (smooth) ; every preset sets every param (a preset load leaves unset keys where they were)
hooks: STD.fx ; mod_drive, mod_bits, mod_downsample STD.mod_in
ui: hero = the engine's own transfer curve (descriptor.curves) + bit staircase, over the output oscilloscope ; knobs in signal order SHAPER · TONE · CRUSH
tests: STD.fx ; bits 1 → output ∈ {−1, +1}·level ; downsample 4 → each value held 4 samples ; silence in → exact silence out ; mix 0.5 impulse = one peak ; auto gain ±6 dB at −18 dBFS full drive, every shape ; low keep keeps a 45 Hz sub ; alias 1 > 4× the fold-over of alias 0

